{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LTJ5DPXR5kdwtQsdHyZ84L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Let me compile the current state:\n\n**Current Performance (fresh measurements):**\n\n| Component | APC 0 | APC 100 | APC 300 | APC 0/300 ratio |\n|-----------|-------|---------|---------|-----------------|\n| STARK excl trace | 2133ms | 1821ms | 1715ms | 1.24x |\n| Constraints | 1300ms | 1243ms | 1240ms | 1.05x |\n\n\n| LogUp GKR | 999ms | 841ms | 755ms | 1.32x |\n| Round 0 | 177ms | 248ms | 300ms | 0.59x (worse) |\n| MLE Rounds | 118ms | 150ms | 183ms | 0.64x (worse) |\n| Openings | 305ms | 238ms | 227ms | 1.34x |\n| WHIR | 218ms | 137ms | 101ms | 2.16x |\n| Stacked Reduction | 83ms | 98ms | 125ms | 0.66x (worse) |\n| Trace Commit | 525ms | 338ms | 246ms | 2.13x |\n\nLooking at the full breakdown, most components scale well with APC increases, but Round 0, MLE Rounds, and Stacked Reduction are actually getting slower—they're moving in the wrong direction. WHIR and Trace Commit show the strongest improvements, scaling over 2x better.\n\nNow I'm checking the STARK numbers at APC 300 and noticing some discrepancy between my fresh measurement of 1715ms and the earlier reported 1517ms. The ~13% variance is within typical GPU benchmark noise, but it's worth noting the measurement uncertainty here.\n\nLooking at the component breakdown, LogUp GKR is the main culprit—jumping from 559ms to 755ms, a 196ms swing that accounts for most of the difference. The other components (Trace Commit and Round 0) are essentially stable. The GKR measurements seem particularly noisy across different runs, ranging from 559ms to 789ms, though the APC 0 baseline is holding steady around 993-999ms.\n\nReviewing the GKR progression across all measurements, the 564ms and 559ms numbers from the multi-stream optimization look suspiciously good compared to the baseline 790ms and the current 755ms reading. The current me