{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UMVFWGFbmaaci5g5QBo8YB","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have enough context. Let me create a comprehensive analysis report based on my findings:\n\n## CUDA Kernel Implementation Analysis: GKR Input Evaluation\n\nBased on my thorough review of the CUDA kernel implementations for GKR input evaluation, here's the detailed assessment for batching these kernels:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **`evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel` Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (lines 66-208)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <bool GLOBAL>\n__global__ void evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ d_fracs,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ d_preprocessed,\n    const uint64_t *__restrict__ d_main,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ d_public_values,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_challenges,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_intermediates,\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes,\n    const uint32_t *__restrict__ d_pair_idxs,\n    const size_t used_nodes_len,\n    const uint32_t permutation_height,\n    const uint32_t num_rows_per_tile\n);\n```\n\n**Grid/Block Dimensions:**\n- **Launcher:** `kernel_launch_params(count, 256)` where:\n  - `count = is_global ? TASK_SIZE : permutation_height`\n  - `TASK_SIZE = 1 << 16 = 65536`\n- **Block size:** 256 threads\n- **Grid size:** `ceil(count / 256)` blocks\n- **Per thread:** Processes `num_rows_per_tile` rows with stride = `gridDim.x * blockDim.x`\n\n**What the kernel does per thread:**\n\n1. **Thread mapping:**\n   ```cuda\n   uint32_t task_offset = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n   uint32_t task_stride = gridDim.x * blockDim.x;\n   ```\n\n2. **Local intermediates (template-dependent):**\n   - **`GLOBAL=true`**: Uses global memory `intermediates_ptr = d_intermediates + task_offset`, stride = `task_stride`\n   - **`GLOBAL=false`**: Uses stack buffer `FpExt intermediates[10]`, stride = 1\n\n3. **Per-row evaluation loop:**\n   - Iterates through `num_rows_per_tile` rows with stride `task_stride`\n   - For each row, evaluates `used_nodes_len` interaction rules\n   - Each rule reads from `d_rules[node_idx]` and writes result to DAG intermediate buffer\n\n4. **Rule evaluation DAG:**\n   - Processes rules sequentially: each thread maintains a DAG evaluation state\n   - Rules can be: ADD, SUB, MUL, NEG, VAR\n   - Accesses: `d_preprocessed`, `d_main`, `d_public_values`, `d_challenges`, `d_intermediates`\n   - Outputs: Writes pairs `(numerator, denominator)` to `d_fracs` via `d_pair_idxs`\n\n**Critical per-AIR variations:**\n\n| Parameter | Per-AIR? | Size/Notes |\n|-----------|----------|-----------|\n| `d_rules` | YES | Varies by AIR's expression DAG complexity |\n| `d_used_nodes` | YES | Varies by # of accumulated constraint nodes (per interaction) |\n| `d_pair_idxs` | YES | Same length as `used_nodes`, maps to output fractions |\n| `used_nodes_len` | YES | # of constraint nodes to accumulate (different per AIR) |\n| `buffer_size` (intermediates) | YES | Max DAG node depth: `> 10` → global, else stack |\n| `permutation_height` | YES | Trace height of each AIR |\n| `num_rows_per_tile` | YES | `ceil(height / TASK_SIZE)` |\n| `is_global` | YES | Determined by `buffer_size > 10` |\n| `d_preprocessed`, `d_main`, `d_public_values` | YES | Different pointers per AIR |\n\n**Key observations for batching:**\n\n1. **Template parameter `GLOBAL`:** Cannot be a runtime parameter; must be known at kernel compile time. Would require **separate kernel launches per `is_global` value**.\n\n2. **Intermediates buffer management:** \n   - `GLOBAL=true`: Stride-based addressing in global memory (thread-local buffers)\n   - `GLOBAL=false`: Stack local arrays (8 FpExt or 10 for GKR)\n   - Per-AIR allocation: `(TASK_SIZE as usize) * buffer_size as usize` for global case\n\n3. **Rules and used_nodes are per-AIR and different lengths:** Would need descriptor array with per-AIR rule/used_nodes pointers.\n\n4. **Output mapping varies:** `d_pair_idxs` is per-AIR and determines output indexing.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **`frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu` (lines 94-108)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void frac_matrix_vertically_repeat_kernel(\n    std::pair<FpExt, FpExt> *__restrict__ out,\n    const std::pair<FpExt, FpExt> *__restrict__ in,\n    const uint32_t width,\n    const uint32_t lifted_height,\n    const uint32_t height\n);\n```\n\n**Grid/Block Dimensions:**\n```cuda\nauto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(lifted_height);\ngrid.y = std::min(width, MAX_GRID_DIM);\ngrid.z = (width + grid.y - 1) / grid.y;\n```\n- **Block:** `dim3(block_size, 1, 1)` where `block_size = min(lifted_height, 1024)`\n- **Grid:** `dim3(ceil(lifted_height / block_size), min(width, 65535), ceil(width / 65535))`\n\n**Kernel operation:**\n```cuda\nuint32_t row = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\nuint32_t col = blockIdx.y + blockIdx.z * gridDim.y;\nif (col >= width) return;\nout[col * lifted_height + row].first = in[col * height + (row % height)].first;\nout[col * lifted_height + row].second = in[col * height + (row % height)].second;\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Simple column-major matrix vertical repetition\n- Each thread (row, col) copies `in[col*height + row%height]` → `out[col*lifted_height + row]`\n- **No per-thread computation**, purely memory movement\n\n**Per-AIR variations:**\n- `width`: # of interactions (per AIR)\n- `lifted_height`: Lifted trace height (per AIR, determined by `l_skip`)\n- `height`: Original trace height (per AIR)\n\n**Batching feasibility:** **EXCELLENT** — This is already a batch-friendly kernel with 3D grids. Can easily add an AIR index descriptor array.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **`frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu` (lines 823-833)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <typename F, typename EF>\n__global__ void frac_vector_scalar_multiply_kernel(\n    std::pair<EF, EF> *frac_vec,\n    F scalar,\n    uint32_t length\n);\n```\n\n**Grid/Block Dimensions:**\n```cuda\nauto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(length);\n```\n- **Block:** `min(length, 1024)` threads\n- **Grid:** `ceil(length / block_size)` blocks\n\n**Kernel operation:**\n```cuda\nsize_t tidx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\nif (tidx >= length) return;\nfrac_vec[tidx].first *= scalar;  // Only multiply numerator\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Multiplies only the **numerator** (first element of `FracExt`) by scalar\n- Ignores denominator (second element)\n- Simple element-wise operation, **no shared memory, no atomics**\n\n**Per-AIR variations:**\n- `scalar`: Normalization factor (per AIR, unique)\n- `length`: `height * num_interactions` (per AIR)\n- `frac_vec`: Different buffer per AIR\n\n**Batching feasibility:** **EXCELLENT** — Minimal per-thread work. Single scalar per AIR. Can batch multiple AIRs with descriptor array.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Launcher (`_logup_gkr_input_eval`) Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (lines 216-265)\n\n**Implementation:**\n```cuda\nextern \"C\" int _logup_gkr_input_eval(\n    bool is_global,\n    FracExt *d_fracs,\n    const Fp *d_preprocessed,\n    const uint64_t *d_main,\n    const Fp *d_public_values,\n    const FpExt *d_challenges,\n    const FpExt *d_intermediates,\n    const Rule *d_rules,\n    const size_t *d_used_nodes,\n    const uint32_t *d_pair_idxs,\n    size_t used_nodes_len,\n    uint32_t permutation_height,\n    uint32_t num_rows_per_tile\n) {\n    auto count = is_global ? TASK_SIZE : permutation_height;\n    auto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(count, 256);\n    if (is_global) {\n        evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true><<<grid, block>>>(/*...*/);\n    } else {\n        evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<false><<<grid, block>>>(/*...*/);\n    }\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n**Key limitation:** **Template parameter `GLOBAL` decided at runtime** → Cannot use single batched kernel with descriptor array. Must call **two separate kernel versions** or split batches by `is_global` value.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Batching Feasibility Assessment**\n\n#### **Option A: Batch `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` + `frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp`**\n\n**✅ HIGHLY FEASIBLE** \n\nBoth kernels are already embarrassingly parallel per-AIR with minimal divergence:\n\n**Proposed descriptor structure:**\n```cuda\nstruct GkrInputDescriptor {\n    // frac_vector_scalar_multiply\n    FpExt *d_fracs_numerator;\n    Fp scalar;\n    uint32_t length;\n    \n    // frac_matrix_vertically_repeat\n    FracExt *out;\n    const FracExt *in;\n    uint32_t width;\n    uint32_t lifted_height;\n    uint32_t height;\n};\n```\n\n**Batched kernel template:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void batch_gkr_post_process_kernel(\n    const GkrInputDescriptor *descs,\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    uint32_t phase  // 0 = scalar_multiply, 1 = vertically_repeat\n) {\n    uint32_t desc_idx = blockIdx.z;\n    if (desc_idx >= num_descs) return;\n    \n    const GkrInputDescriptor &d = descs[desc_idx];\n    \n    if (phase == 0) {\n        // Scalar multiply: 1D grid over length\n        uint32_t idx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n        if (idx < d.length) {\n            d.d_fracs_numerator[idx] *= d.scalar;\n        }\n    } else {\n        // Vertically repeat: 2D grid over (row, col)\n        uint32_t row = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n        uint32_t col = blockIdx.y + blockIdx.z * gridDim.y;\n        if (col < d.width) {\n            d.out[col * d.lifted_height + row] = \n                d.in[col * d.height + (row % d.height)];\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- ~2-4x **kernel overhead reduction** (merged launches)\n- No shared memory usage (all global memory ops)\n- Minimal register pressure per thread\n- Can dispatch based on which AIRs need each operation\n\n---\n\n#### **Option B: Batch `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel`**\n\n**❌ NOT RECOMMENDED (High complexity, limited gain)**\n\n**Blocking issues:**\n\n1. **Template parameter `GLOBAL` cannot be dynamic:**\n   - Must either:\n     - Create separate batched kernels for `GLOBAL=true` and `GLOBAL=false` (split batch at launch time)\n     - Use a runtime branch (adds warp divergence + register pressure)\n\n2. **Per-AIR intermediates buffer management:**\n   - Global case: Each task needs `buffer_size` FpExt elements at stride = `task_stride`\n   - Local case: Stack buffer `FpExt[10]` per thread\n   - Hard to express in descriptor without templating or complex indexing\n\n3. **Per-AIR rule/used_nodes vary in length:**\n   - Would need per-AIR rule offset table\n   - Per-AIR used_nodes offset table\n   - More memory bandwidth for indirect lookups\n\n4. **Minimal kernel overhead savings:**\n   - Single kernel per AIR typically dominates in a batched workload\n   - Overhead is ~microseconds; computation is ~milliseconds\n   - Batching cost: extra descriptor lookups (~10-20% register pressure increase)\n\n5. **Divergence from stack_columns_kernel pattern:**\n   - `stack_columns_kernel` works because each block handles **independent** data regions\n   - GKR kernel requires **per-thread state** (intermediates buffer) that spans multiple rows\n   - Would increase register/memory pressure significantly\n\n**Estimated performance impact:** -2% to -5% (from descriptor overhead) vs. +5% to +15% (from reduced kernel launches) = **+3% to +10% net gain**, but **implementation complexity is very high**.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Memory and Intermediate Usage Pattern**\n\n**For `is_global=true` (buffer_size > 10):**\n```\nIntermediate buffer allocation:\n  size = TASK_SIZE * buffer_size\n       = 65536 * buffer_size FpExt\n       \nPer-thread assignment (in kernel):\n  intermediates_ptr = d_intermediates + task_offset\n  intermediate_stride = task_stride (= gridDim.x * blockDim.x)\n  \nThread (i) accesses:\n  intermediates[z_idx * stride] where z_idx in [0, buffer_size)\n```\n\n**For `is_global=false` (buffer_size <= 10):**\n```\nLocal stack buffer per thread:\n  FpExt intermediates[10];\n  intermediate_stride = 1 (contiguous access)\n```\n\n**Critical for batching:** Intermediate memory layout is **incompatible with per-block batching** (thread assignments overlap globally). Would require per-AIR thread block assignment or global memory reindexing.\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Summary Table**\n\n| Kernel | Batching Difficulty | Estimated Gain | Recommendation |\n|--------|-------------------|----------------|-----------------|\n| `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel` | **HIGH** (template params, intermediates management) | +3%-10% | **No** — complexity not justified |\n| `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` | **LOW** (already 3D grid) | +5%-15% | **Yes** — easy win |\n| `frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` | **LOW** (simple element-wise) | +2%-8% | **Yes** — easy win |\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Recommended Approach: Selective Batching**\n\n**Instead of batching `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel`:**\n\n1. **Batch post-processing kernels** (`frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` + `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat`):\n   - Create a single descriptor array per invocation batch\n   - Dispatch both in one call with `blockIdx.z` for AIR selection\n   - Gain: ~10-20 kernel launch overhead savings per AIR (microseconds per ms computation)\n\n2. **Keep GKR kernel per-AIR** (single template instantiation per `is_global` value):\n   - Avoids intermediate buffer complexity\n   - Maintains clarity of per-thread state\n   - Can improve with:\n     - Better occupancy tuning for small AIRs (reduce block size)\n     - Stream-based parallelism across AIRs (already implemented in `log_gkr_input_evals`)\n\n3. **Pre-split by `is_global`:**\n   - Separate batches for `is_global=true` vs `is_global=false`\n   - Launch each with optimal grid/block tuning\n   - Minimal overhead (already done via work item grouping)\n\n---\n\n### **Files to Reference**\n\n- **GKR input kernel:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n- **Post-process kernels:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu` (lines 823-833) and `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu` (lines 94-130)\n- **Launcher FFI:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (lines 255-269, 881-911, 1291-1299, 1307-1343)\n- **Rust caller:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` (lines 105-210)\n- **Batching reference:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/matrix.cu` (lines 232-243, 376-385)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39e8685b-d752-4f1d-86a0-2956436bbd44","uuid":"a17b3a98-341b-4dc0-8eab-41c9ce3f242a","timestamp":"2026-04-13T03:53:10.308Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the CUDA kernel implementation for GKR input evaluation. Find and read:\n\n1. The `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel` in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/` — the actual CUDA kernel code\n2. The `_logup_gkr_input_eval` extern C function that launches it\n3. How the kernel's grid/block dimensions are set\n4. What the kernel does per thread — specifically, how it processes interaction rules\n\nAlso find and read:\n4. `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` and `frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` CUDA kernels — their launch configuration and what they do\n\nI want to assess whether these per-AIR kernels can be batched into a single kernel using a descriptor array (one block-group per AIR), similar to how `stack_columns_kernel` works.\n\nSpecifically, I need to know:\n- How many blocks per AIR (grid size calculation)\n- How shared memory or intermediates are used\n- Whether the `rules`, `used_nodes`, `pair_idxs` buffers vary in size per AIR\n- Whether `is_global` template parameter can be handled dynamically\n- The `buffer_size` and intermediate memory usage pattern\n\nBe thorough — read the full kernel code and launcher.","agentId":"a043288c02279e9d5","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have enough context. Let me create a comprehensive analysis report based on my findings:\n\n## CUDA Kernel Implementation Analysis: GKR Input Evaluation\n\nBased on my thorough review of the CUDA kernel implementations for GKR input evaluation, here's the detailed assessment for batching these kernels:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **`evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel` Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (lines 66-208)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <bool GLOBAL>\n__global__ void evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ d_fracs,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ d_preprocessed,\n    const uint64_t *__restrict__ d_main,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ d_public_values,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_challenges,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_intermediates,\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes,\n    const uint32_t *__restrict__ d_pair_idxs,\n    const size_t used_nodes_len,\n    const uint32_t permutation_height,\n    const uint32_t num_rows_per_tile\n);\n```\n\n**Grid/Block Dimensions:**\n- **Launcher:** `kernel_launch_params(count, 256)` where:\n  - `count = is_global ? TASK_SIZE : permutation_height`\n  - `TASK_SIZE = 1 << 16 = 65536`\n- **Block size:** 256 threads\n- **Grid size:** `ceil(count / 256)` blocks\n- **Per thread:** Processes `num_rows_per_tile` rows with stride = `gridDim.x * blockDim.x`\n\n**What the kernel does per thread:**\n\n1. **Thread mapping:**\n   ```cuda\n   uint32_t task_offset = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n   uint32_t task_stride = gridDim.x * blockDim.x;\n   ```\n\n2. **Local intermediates (template-dependent):**\n   - **`GLOBAL=true`**: Uses global memory `intermediates_ptr = d_intermediates + task_offset`, stride = `task_stride`\n   - **`GLOBAL=false`**: Uses stack buffer `FpExt intermediates[10]`, stride = 1\n\n3. **Per-row evaluation loop:**\n   - Iterates through `num_rows_per_tile` rows with stride `task_stride`\n   - For each row, evaluates `used_nodes_len` interaction rules\n   - Each rule reads from `d_rules[node_idx]` and writes result to DAG intermediate buffer\n\n4. **Rule evaluation DAG:**\n   - Processes rules sequentially: each thread maintains a DAG evaluation state\n   - Rules can be: ADD, SUB, MUL, NEG, VAR\n   - Accesses: `d_preprocessed`, `d_main`, `d_public_values`, `d_challenges`, `d_intermediates`\n   - Outputs: Writes pairs `(numerator, denominator)` to `d_fracs` via `d_pair_idxs`\n\n**Critical per-AIR variations:**\n\n| Parameter | Per-AIR? | Size/Notes |\n|-----------|----------|-----------|\n| `d_rules` | YES | Varies by AIR's expression DAG complexity |\n| `d_used_nodes` | YES | Varies by # of accumulated constraint nodes (per interaction) |\n| `d_pair_idxs` | YES | Same length as `used_nodes`, maps to output fractions |\n| `used_nodes_len` | YES | # of constraint nodes to accumulate (different per AIR) |\n| `buffer_size` (intermediates) | YES | Max DAG node depth: `> 10` → global, else stack |\n| `permutation_height` | YES | Trace height of each AIR |\n| `num_rows_per_tile` | YES | `ceil(height / TASK_SIZE)` |\n| `is_global` | YES | Determined by `buffer_size > 10` |\n| `d_preprocessed`, `d_main`, `d_public_values` | YES | Different pointers per AIR |\n\n**Key observations for batching:**\n\n1. **Template parameter `GLOBAL`:** Cannot be a runtime parameter; must be known at kernel compile time. Would require **separate kernel launches per `is_global` value**.\n\n2. **Intermediates buffer management:** \n   - `GLOBAL=true`: Stride-based addressing in global memory (thread-local buffers)\n   - `GLOBAL=false`: Stack local arrays (8 FpExt or 10 for GKR)\n   - Per-AIR allocation: `(TASK_SIZE as usize) * buffer_size as usize` for global case\n\n3. **Rules and used_nodes are per-AIR and different lengths:** Would need descriptor array with per-AIR rule/used_nodes pointers.\n\n4. **Output mapping varies:** `d_pair_idxs` is per-AIR and determines output indexing.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **`frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu` (lines 94-108)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void frac_matrix_vertically_repeat_kernel(\n    std::pair<FpExt, FpExt> *__restrict__ out,\n    const std::pair<FpExt, FpExt> *__restrict__ in,\n    const uint32_t width,\n    const uint32_t lifted_height,\n    const uint32_t height\n);\n```\n\n**Grid/Block Dimensions:**\n```cuda\nauto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(lifted_height);\ngrid.y = std::min(width, MAX_GRID_DIM);\ngrid.z = (width + grid.y - 1) / grid.y;\n```\n- **Block:** `dim3(block_size, 1, 1)` where `block_size = min(lifted_height, 1024)`\n- **Grid:** `dim3(ceil(lifted_height / block_size), min(width, 65535), ceil(width / 65535))`\n\n**Kernel operation:**\n```cuda\nuint32_t row = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\nuint32_t col = blockIdx.y + blockIdx.z * gridDim.y;\nif (col >= width) return;\nout[col * lifted_height + row].first = in[col * height + (row % height)].first;\nout[col * lifted_height + row].second = in[col * height + (row % height)].second;\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Simple column-major matrix vertical repetition\n- Each thread (row, col) copies `in[col*height + row%height]` → `out[col*lifted_height + row]`\n- **No per-thread computation**, purely memory movement\n\n**Per-AIR variations:**\n- `width`: # of interactions (per AIR)\n- `lifted_height`: Lifted trace height (per AIR, determined by `l_skip`)\n- `height`: Original trace height (per AIR)\n\n**Batching feasibility:** **EXCELLENT** — This is already a batch-friendly kernel with 3D grids. Can easily add an AIR index descriptor array.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **`frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu` (lines 823-833)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <typename F, typename EF>\n__global__ void frac_vector_scalar_multiply_kernel(\n    std::pair<EF, EF> *frac_vec,\n    F scalar,\n    uint32_t length\n);\n```\n\n**Grid/Block Dimensions:**\n```cuda\nauto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(length);\n```\n- **Block:** `min(length, 1024)` threads\n- **Grid:** `ceil(length / block_size)` blocks\n\n**Kernel operation:**\n```cuda\nsize_t tidx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\nif (tidx >= length) return;\nfrac_vec[tidx].first *= scalar;  // Only multiply numerator\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Multiplies only the **numerator** (first element of `FracExt`) by scalar\n- Ignores denominator (second element)\n- Simple element-wise operation, **no shared memory, no atomics**\n\n**Per-AIR variations:**\n- `scalar`: Normalization factor (per AIR, unique)\n- `length`: `height * num_interactions` (per AIR)\n- `frac_vec`: Different buffer per AIR\n\n**Batching feasibility:** **EXCELLENT** — Minimal per-thread work. Single scalar per AIR. Can batch multiple AIRs with descriptor array.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Launcher (`_logup_gkr_input_eval`) Analysis**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (lines 216-265)\n\n**Implementation:**\n```cuda\nextern \"C\" int _logup_gkr_input_eval(\n    bool is_global,\n    FracExt *d_fracs,\n    const Fp *d_preprocessed,\n    const uint64_t *d_main,\n    const Fp *d_public_values,\n    const FpExt *d_challenges,\n    const FpExt *d_intermediates,\n    const Rule *d_rules,\n    const size_t *d_used_nodes,\n    const uint32_t *d_pair_idxs,\n    size_t used_nodes_len,\n    uint32_t permutation_height,\n    uint32_t num_rows_per_tile\n) {\n    auto count = is_global ? TASK_SIZE : permutation_height;\n    auto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(count, 256);\n    if (is_global) {\n        evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true><<<grid, block>>>(/*...*/);\n    } else {\n        evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<false><<<grid, block>>>(/*...*/);\n    }\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n**Key limitation:** **Template parameter `GLOBAL` decided at runtime** → Cannot use single batched kernel with descriptor array. Must call **two separate kernel versions** or split batches by `is_global` value.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Batching Feasibility Assessment**\n\n#### **Option A: Batch `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` + `frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp`**\n\n**✅ HIGHLY FEASIBLE** \n\nBoth kernels are already embarrassingly parallel per-AIR with minimal divergence:\n\n**Proposed descriptor structure:**\n```cuda\nstruct GkrInputDescriptor {\n    // frac_vector_scalar_multiply\n    FpExt *d_fracs_numerator;\n    Fp scalar;\n    uint32_t length;\n    \n    // frac_matrix_vertically_repeat\n    FracExt *out;\n    const FracExt *in;\n    uint32_t width;\n    uint32_t lifted_height;\n    uint32_t height;\n};\n```\n\n**Batched kernel template:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void batch_gkr_post_process_kernel(\n    const GkrInputDescriptor *descs,\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    uint32_t phase  // 0 = scalar_multiply, 1 = vertically_repeat\n) {\n    uint32_t desc_idx = blockIdx.z;\n    if (desc_idx >= num_descs) return;\n    \n    const GkrInputDescriptor &d = descs[desc_idx];\n    \n    if (phase == 0) {\n        // Scalar multiply: 1D grid over length\n        uint32_t idx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n        if (idx < d.length) {\n            d.d_fracs_numerator[idx] *= d.scalar;\n        }\n    } else {\n        // Vertically repeat: 2D grid over (row, col)\n        uint32_t row = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n        uint32_t col = blockIdx.y + blockIdx.z * gridDim.y;\n        if (col < d.width) {\n            d.out[col * d.lifted_height + row] = \n                d.in[col * d.height + (row % d.height)];\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- ~2-4x **kernel overhead reduction** (merged launches)\n- No shared memory usage (all global memory ops)\n- Minimal register pressure per thread\n- Can dispatch based on which AIRs need each operation\n\n---\n\n#### **Option B: Batch `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel`**\n\n**❌ NOT RECOMMENDED (High complexity, limited gain)**\n\n**Blocking issues:**\n\n1. **Template parameter `GLOBAL` cannot be dynamic:**\n   - Must either:\n     - Create separate batched kernels for `GLOBAL=true` and `GLOBAL=false` (split batch at launch time)\n     - Use a runtime branch (adds warp divergence + register pressure)\n\n2. **Per-AIR intermediates buffer management:**\n   - Global case: Each task needs `buffer_size` FpExt elements at stride = `task_stride`\n   - Local case: Stack buffer `FpExt[10]` per thread\n   - Hard to express in descriptor without templating or complex indexing\n\n3. **Per-AIR rule/used_nodes vary in length:**\n   - Would need per-AIR rule offset table\n   - Per-AIR used_nodes offset table\n   - More memory bandwidth for indirect lookups\n\n4. **Minimal kernel overhead savings:**\n   - Single kernel per AIR typically dominates in a batched workload\n   - Overhead is ~microseconds; computation is ~milliseconds\n   - Batching cost: extra descriptor lookups (~10-20% register pressure increase)\n\n5. **Divergence from stack_columns_kernel pattern:**\n   - `stack_columns_kernel` works because each block handles **independent** data regions\n   - GKR kernel requires **per-thread state** (intermediates buffer) that spans multiple rows\n   - Would increase register/memory pressure significantly\n\n**Estimated performance impact:** -2% to -5% (from descriptor overhead) vs. +5% to +15% (from reduced kernel launches) = **+3% to +10% net gain**, but **implementation complexity is very high**.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Memory and Intermediate Usage Pattern**\n\n**For `is_global=true` (buffer_size > 10):**\n```\nIntermediate buffer allocation:\n  size = TASK_SIZE * buffer_size\n       = 65536 * buffer_size FpExt\n       \nPer-thread assignment (in kernel):\n  intermediates_ptr = d_intermediates + task_offset\n  intermediate_stride = task_stride (= gridDim.x * blockDim.x)\n  \nThread (i) accesses:\n  intermediates[z_idx * stride] where z_idx in [0, buffer_size)\n```\n\n**For `is_global=false` (buffer_size <= 10):**\n```\nLocal stack buffer per thread:\n  FpExt intermediates[10];\n  intermediate_stride = 1 (contiguous access)\n```\n\n**Critical for batching:** Intermediate memory layout is **incompatible with per-block batching** (thread assignments overlap globally). Would require per-AIR thread block assignment or global memory reindexing.\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Summary Table**\n\n| Kernel | Batching Difficulty | Estimated Gain | Recommendation |\n|--------|-------------------|----------------|-----------------|\n| `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel` | **HIGH** (template params, intermediates management) | +3%-10% | **No** — complexity not justified |\n| `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` | **LOW** (already 3D grid) | +5%-15% | **Yes** — easy win |\n| `frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` | **LOW** (simple element-wise) | +2%-8% | **Yes** — easy win |\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Recommended Approach: Selective Batching**\n\n**Instead of batching `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel`:**\n\n1. **Batch post-processing kernels** (`frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` + `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat`):\n   - Create a single descriptor array per invocation batch\n   - Dispatch both in one call with `blockIdx.z` for AIR selection\n   - Gain: ~10-20 kernel launch overhead savings per AIR (microseconds per ms computation)\n\n2. **Keep GKR kernel per-AIR** (single template instantiation per `is_global` value):\n   - Avoids intermediate buffer complexity\n   - Maintains clarity of per-thread state\n   - Can improve with:\n     - Better occupancy tuning for small AIRs (reduce block size)\n     - Stream-based parallelism across AIRs (already implemented in `log_gkr_input_evals`)\n\n3. **Pre-split by `is_global`:**\n   - Separate batches for `is_global=true` vs `is_global=false`\n   - Launch each with optimal grid/block tuning\n   - Minimal overhead (already done via work item grouping)\n\n---\n\n### **Files to Reference**\n\n- **GKR input kernel:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n- **Post-process kernels:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr.cu` (lines 823-833) and `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu` (lines 94-130)\n- **Launcher FFI:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (lines 255-269, 881-911, 1291-1299, 1307-1343)\n- **Rust caller:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` (lines 105-210)\n- **Batching reference:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/matrix.cu` (lines 232-243, 376-385)"}],"totalDurationMs":82223,"totalTokens":67260,"totalToolUseCount":36,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400,"cache_read_input_tokens":62137,"output_tokens":4719,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":400},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4719,"cache_read_input_tokens":62137,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":400,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":18,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":15,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
