{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019bVunQ8c1xiAfUsFFVH7ET","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DcnFjh31XpTTmmBWLb2gP3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers\n\nPre-allocate per-thread reusable GPU buffers for GKR input evaluation to eliminate per-AIR memory management overhead and unlock multi-stream concurrency. Currently, each of the ~310 per-segment AIRs allocates and frees an `intermediates` DeviceBuffer through the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>`, which also calls `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` on the per-thread CUDA stream pool. This serializes the 8 worker threads via both the Rust mutex and implicit CUDA pool synchronization, producing ~1.0x effective parallelism (529ms wall for 471ms GPU kernel time). Pre-allocating max-sized buffers per thread before spawning workers should eliminate ~2500 lock acquisitions per segment and all per-AIR CUDA pool operations, enabling real kernel concurrency and targeting a 1.5–2.5x reduction in GKR input eval wall time.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1682,"cache_read_input_tokens":149025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1682},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39e8685b-d752-4f1d-86a0-2956436bbd44","uuid":"8c21f19f-35f7-4dac-a963-124d9ac2e8ca"}
