{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a3bd9a7c7e0879227","tool_use_id":"toolu_015up8qi3WWG2VDDCSpNUXqA","description":"Review optimization plan (round 2)","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Review this updated optimization plan following the review guideline. This is the second review round — a previous review identified issues that have been addressed. Return your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n\nRead the following files:\n\n1. `autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard\n2. `autoopt/context.md` — project context  \n3. `autoopt-results/task.md` — the task\n4. `autoopt-results/2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers/plan.md` — the updated plan\n\nThen verify key claims against the codebase:\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` — the file being modified (full file)\n- Read `crates/cuda-common/src/copy.rs` — verify `copy_to` works for the proposed usage\n- Read `crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs` lines 1-90 — verify DeviceBuffer::with_capacity behavior\n- Check that `tmp.len()` is indeed used as a parameter at line 198 in gkr_input.rs\n\nPrevious review findings that should be resolved:\n1. The unnecessary `copy_into_device_buffer` helper was removed — plan now uses existing `copy_to`\n2. Public values null-pointer case is now handled explicitly\n3. DeviceBuffer capacity/length confusion was corrected\n4. Memory budget safety valve is now concrete (halve num_threads if >2GB)\n5. `tmp.len()` issue addressed — plan proposes passing `height * num_interactions` instead\n\nCheck if these fixes are correct and if any new issues were introduced. Also verify:\n- Is the `frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` fix at line 198 correct? The current code uses `tmp.len()` — does the proposed change to pass `height * num_interactions` produce the correct result?\n- Does the `copy_to` check (`self.len() > dst.len()`) work correctly when source is smaller than destination?\n- Are there any other functions